  "body": "First functional Gen-4 feature wired into an in-browser demo (the deeper rebuild you OK'd) \u2014 **the scheduled heartbeat**, in `Mantle_Spreadsheet_Agent.html`. Not just descriptive prose: the organism can now plan a wake on a **future beat** to chain a thought / run a task only as often as it needs, staying asleep until due \u2014 matching the framework's `Heart.schedule_pulse`.\n\n- `state.scheduledPulses` queue; `schedulePulse()` / `cancelPulse()` helpers.\n- `heartbeat()` fires any due pulse as a **SIGNIFICANT** `scheduled_pulse` sense (the MIND attends it), one-shot; `classifyEvent` marks it SIGNIFICANT.\n- Body primitives **`heart.schedule({reason, after|at})`** / **`heart.cancel({reason})`** (added to `ZOMBIE_PRIMITIVES`, handled in `executeZombiePrimitive`) \u2014 the MIND-callable command path.\n- `ORGAN_ATLAS` Heart entry updated (`implementedBy` + SCHED-1 audit note).\n\n**Browser-verified via the preview harness:** scheduled 3 beats out \u2192 slept beats 1\u20132 \u2192 fired once on beat 3 with the right reason + `scheduled` flag \u2192 one-shot; `heart.schedule`/`heart.cancel` work; the demo's own **Stage-1 self-audit still PASSES**; zero console errors.\n\n(CI here only exercises the Python package + standalone cube; the demo is verified in-browser.)\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
